  "source": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Scroll-Driven Progress</title>\n  <script type=\"application/json\" id=\"effect-meta\">\n  {\n    \"id\": \"scroll-driven-progress\",\n    \"title\": \"Scroll-Driven Progress\",\n    \"summary\": \"A bar driven by native scroll-timeline.\",\n    \"description\": \"A bar driven by native scroll-timeline.\",\n    \"theme\": \"scroll-effects\",\n    \"categories\": [\"scroll\", \"motion\"],\n    \"tags\": [\"scroll\", \"scroll-timeline\", \"progress\", \"native\", \"css-only\"],\n    \"tech\": [\"css\"],\n    \"era\": \"2020s\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"intermediate\",\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"browser_support\": \"All modern browsers (Chromium, Firefox, Safari).\",\n    \"performance_notes\": \"Lightweight — composited transform/opacity work only.\",\n    \"accessibility_notes\": \"Scroll-linked motion must be disabled under prefers-reduced-motion, and content must never depend on scrolling to become readable.\",\n    \"customization\": [\n      { \"name\": \"--c\", \"description\": \"Bar colour\", \"default\": \"#7c5cff\" }\n    ],\n    \"variations\": [\"Retune through the custom properties\", \"Add a reduced-motion static variant\"],\n    \"ai_usage\": \"Reading progress. animation-timeline: scroll() runs on the compositor with no JS listener; keep a JS fallback for browsers without scroll-driven animation support.\"\n  }\n  </script>\n  <style>\n    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; }\n    body { background: #0b0d12; color: #e7ebf3;\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif; }\n    body { min-height: 260vh; background: linear-gradient(#0b0d12, #1a1030); }\n    .bar { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 5px; transform-origin: left; background: #7c5cff;\n      animation: grow linear; animation-timeline: scroll(root); scale: 0 1; }\n    .content { padding: 30vh 1.5rem; color: #cbd5e1; max-width: 34ch; }\n    h2 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; }\n    p { color: #8b93a7; line-height: 1.6; }\n    @keyframes grow { to { scale: 1 1; } }\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n      .bar { animation: none; scale: 1 1; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"bar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n  <div class=\"content\"><h2>Scroll to fill the bar</h2><p>The progress bar is driven entirely by CSS scroll-timeline — no scroll listener, no layout thrash.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"content\"><h2>Still scrolling</h2><p>Because it runs on the compositor, the bar never lags behind fast flicks.</p></div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
